// examples/snake.ent, a game in ent-lang only: the snake's pieces are
// entities that are counted (`let n = for ...`) to see what the head
// runs into and where food can go, in a `loop` that looks until it finds
// a free cell. Run without a window for three frames: the board, as big
// as fits in the window, and what it says before a game.
// RUN: sh %S/Inputs/headless.sh %t.dir
// RUN: sed 's/until Window.closed/until Window.frame > 2/' \
// RUN:     %S/../../examples/snake.ent > %t.snake.ent
// RUN: %ent run -I %t.dir %t.snake.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// (960 by 720: cells of 38, 24 by 16 of them.)
// CHECK:      rounded 18 70 924 620 by 8 8 8 8 002a3442
// CHECK-NEXT: rect 24 76 912 608 00161c24
// CHECK:      label 24 18 "score 0"
// CHECK:      "snake"
// CHECK:      "space to start; arrows turn, F fills the screen"
